Z||000010||frontal lobe||10-11-2000||11:59 PM||||Ah, Patrick.  I'm with you.  The demise of the english language.<P>Here's a pet peeve of mine--the common use now of nouns or adjectives as verbs.  Example:  It "impacted" me in such and such a way.  In my line of work "impacted" had a very different meaning than "had an impact".  So now when someone says they were impacted by something, I have to fight the imagery produced.<P>By the way, I try to give people a little more slack on the forum because we are writing in a conversational format and not always proper english.  Still, even cutting slack, I know what you mean.||||reg||1
